From 68b5cd6b3080717bc56ce660405b83af025582cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:46:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Teleother, all three, and the Accept aid setting nothing had
 ever read

tools/unwiredspells.json said of Teleother Lumbridge, Falador and
Camelot that they need "the teleother accept/decline dialogue and target
consent - none of that exists yet". The dialogue existed. inter_251.if
is Jagex's own Teleport Option panel: the caster's name, "...wants to
teleport you to...", the destination, "Do you accept?", Accept and
Decline, with the teleother models already animating in two corners.
The buttons in magic.if were fully drawn too - buttontype=target,
actiontarget=npc,player, and the real rune and level checks. What was
missing was the flow, not the screen, and not the numbers.

Fourth time a "does not exist" note has been wrong, after Trollheim,
Ape Atoll and the ancient spellbook.

NOT ONE NUMBER WAS TYPED FROM A WIKI. Every level and every rune count
on the three new magic_spell_table rows is re-derived from the cache's
own button scripts by teleother_battery.py - script4=gt,73 is level 74,
script1=gt,1 on soulrune is two souls - and compared. The client has
been greying these spells correctly since the unpack; only the server
did not know the numbers. Each row's tele_coord is asserted equal to the
ordinary teleport to that town. Experience is the one figure no button
carries, so it is OSRS's and is labelled as such.

THE PANEL WENT THROUGH tools/genadopt.py, the adoption tool the windows
round added an hour earlier, rather than a second hand rename beside it.
Four rules in adoptspec.json name accept, decline, caster and
destination off the panel's own text, everything else keeps its com_<n>,
and windows_battery's "re-running the generators changes nothing" now
covers this panel too. %1 and %2 say nothing about what they hold, so
the join is positional - and the battery asserts the position by y
coordinate: the caster slot is above the "...wants to teleport you to..."
line and the destination below it.

THE COST IS PAID ON CAST, win or lose (Corey's call, and OSRS's). Every
reason not to cast is checked first; from the delete_spell_runes line
on, the runes are spent whatever the answer is. The wilderness rule is
the ordinary teleport rule and is asked of both coords, so you cannot
stand at level 1 and pull somebody out of level 40.

CLOSING THE WINDOW IS DECLINING. Being attacked closes a modal, and an
offer left standing after its panel is gone is an offer that can still
teleport somebody ten seconds later from wherever the fight moved them.
So [if_close] is the decline, the Decline button is nothing but a close,
and Accept consumes the offer BEFORE it closes anything. The offer
expires after 17 ticks, and the accept path re-checks that itself rather
than trusting the softtimer to have fired.

ACCEPT AID WAS ALREADY THERE AND ALREADY BROKEN. %option_aid is a perm
varp with a Yes/No pair drawn in both options tabs, and nothing in the
build had ever read it - while options:com_52 and com_53, the Accept Aid
pair, set %option_pm. So "Accept Aid: Yes" silently turned your Split
Private-chat on and left aid alone. The low-detail tab had it right.
Both are fixed, and the varp is now a tri-state (0 unset / 1 yes /
2 no) with the Yes button lighting on lt,2: a varp has no default, every
existing save holds 0, and 0 has to mean accepting or this spell would
fail for everybody on the day it ships. It was also a display fix - a
player who had never touched the setting had neither Yes nor No lit.

Tele Block stays in unwiredspells.json and is now the only entry left.
Its note is the accurate kind: it needs a teleport-blocked timer every
teleport path honours, which is a mechanism, not a panel. enchant_battery
pinned that file at five entries; the pin moves to two, and its wording
no longer carries the number, because a count inside a check's message
is a mutation label that has to be edited in two files every time it
moves.

62 mutations, all caught by their own check. rs2check 0/0, every battery
ALL PASS except poh's group 64b, which needs a build as always. Not
built here: npm and bun both still 403 on this sandbox's registry, so
CI's pack job is the build.

